    "contenu": "\n      <p>How much does <strong>corporate catering in Paris</strong> cost? The honest answer: at L'Écrin Traiteur, <strong>from €6 to €52 per person excl. VAT</strong> depending on the service, from the afternoon break to the dinner reception, and on quote for a bespoke reception. But what really makes the difference is what you pay for, and what you do not see on the invoice.</p>\n\n      <h2>Our prices by service, 2026 reference table</h2>\n      <table>\n        <thead>\n          <tr>\n            <th>Service</th>\n            <th>Price / person excl. VAT (low)</th>\n            <th>Price / person excl. VAT (high)</th>\n            <th>What explains the difference</th>\n          </tr>\n        </thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr>\n            <td><strong>Breakfast</strong> (Classique formula to full breakfast)</td>\n            <td>€8</td>\n            <td>€16</td>\n            <td>Classique: pastries, juice, coffee, fruit. Full: madeleines or cakes, farmhouse yoghurts, a wider selection of juices</td>\n          </tr>\n          <tr>\n            <td><strong>Afternoon break</strong> (corporate afternoon snack)</td>\n            <td>€6</td>\n            <td>€15</td>\n            <td>A simple break (cookies or madeleines + a drink) or premium (macarons, tartlets, fresh fruit, hot drinks)</td>\n          </tr>\n          <tr>\n            <td><strong>Individual lunch tray</strong></td>\n            <td>€28.90</td>\n            <td>€30.90</td>\n            <td>Vegetarian, chicken or salmon menu; starter, main, dessert and bread included</td>\n          </tr>\n          <tr>\n            <td><strong>Sharing menu</strong></td>\n            <td>€34.90</td>\n            <td>€37.90</td>\n            <td>Menu sized for 8 to 12 people, chosen from several recipes</td>\n          </tr>\n          <tr>\n            <td><strong>Cocktail reception</strong> (8, 12 or 16 canapés)</td>\n            <td>€29.90</td>\n            <td>€51.90</td>\n            <td>Number of canapés per person: L'Invitation, La Réception, La Célébration</td>\n          </tr>\n          <tr>\n            <td><strong>Bespoke reception</strong></td>\n            <td>On quote</td>\n            <td>On quote</td>\n            <td>Format, headcount, live cooking stations and venue</td>\n          </tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n      <p>Delivery €29 excl. VAT in Paris and nearby towns, €50 minimum order (excl. VAT), company invoicing with VAT.</p>\n\n      <h2>What quotes do not always show</h2>\n      <p>When you compare catering quotes in Paris, watch out for <strong>hidden costs</strong> that blow up the final bill:</p>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Delivery charges</strong>, from €15 to €60 depending on the area and the caterer. L'Écrin Traiteur states its charge from the quote: €29 excl. VAT in Paris and nearby towns.</li>\n        <li><strong>Tableware</strong>, plates, cutlery and napkins can add €3 to €8 per person.</li>\n        <li><strong>The minimum order</strong>, some caterers require a minimum of €200 to €500. L'Écrin Traiteur starts at €50 excl. VAT.</li>\n        <li><strong>Service charges</strong>, for cocktail receptions and buffets, some caterers charge waiting staff separately (€80 to €150 per waiter per hour).</li>\n        <li><strong>VAT</strong>, food is charged at 5.5% or 10% depending on the product, but the service itself may be at 20%. Always check the VAT breakdown on the quote.</li>\n      </ul>\n\n      <h2>How to optimise your corporate catering budget</h2>\n      <p>Three practical levers to keep the quality while controlling costs:</p>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Choose the right format</strong>, a Classique formula at €8 per person excl. VAT can replace a sharing menu at €34.90 per person excl. VAT for a 45-minute meeting. Compare our <a href=\"/creations/plateaux-repas\">lunch trays</a> and our <a href=\"/creations/cocktails\">cocktail receptions and buffets</a> to match the format to the occasion. Think about the format before the caterer.</li>\n        <li><strong>Order ahead</strong>, ordering before 2 pm the day before avoids the \"last minute\" surcharges some caterers apply. From 50 people or for several sites, 48 hours' notice is recommended.</li>\n        <li><strong>Work with a specialist caterer</strong>, a specialist <a href=\"/traiteur\">corporate caterer</a> (such as L'Écrin Traiteur) will be cheaper and better than a general caterer for this type of service. Specialisation makes it possible to optimise volumes and logistics.</li>\n      </ul>\n\n      <h2>Request a tailored quote within 24 hours</h2>\n      <p>From a tray of pastries to a <a href=\"/creations/cocktails\">dinner reception</a>, each budget matches a specific format: it is up to you to choose the one that serves your occasion. Explore our <a href=\"/traiteur\">corporate catering</a> offer and <a href=\"/devis\">request your quote</a> for clear pricing, a detailed VAT breakdown and no hidden costs. Delivery from 6:30 am in Paris and Île-de-France, reply within 24 hours.</p>\n      <p>Update, October 2026: the prices shown are catalogue prices. The rule remains an order until 2 pm the day before, with 48 hours' notice recommended from 50 people or for several sites.</p>\n        ",
